<Docs
  title="Trademarks"
  description="What the MIT licence does and does not cover when using logos from the FinMarks dataset."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Contributing</p>
  <h1>Trademarks</h1>

  <p class="intro">
    The MIT licence covers <strong>this repository's code, schemas and metadata</strong>. It does
    <strong>not</strong> cover the logos. Every mark distributed here belongs to its owner. Nothing
    about this repository transfers, dilutes, or licenses those rights.
  </p>


  <h2>What that means in practice</h2>

  <p>
    Reproducing a logo to <strong>identify the thing it names</strong> is normally fine. That is
    nominative use, and it is why a comparison table can show competitor logos and why your app can
    show a bank's mark next to a linked account.
  </p>

  <h3>Typical safe uses</h3>

  <ul>
    <li>Showing a bank's logo beside a user's linked account</li>
    <li>A payment method picker displaying UPI app icons</li>
    <li>An account aggregator consent screen naming the FIP</li>
    <li>Documentation or a comparison table referring to real providers</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Typical unsafe uses</h3>

  <ul>
    <li>Putting a bank's logo on your marketing site in a way that implies partnership</li>
    <li>Using a mark in your own logo, product name, app icon, or domain</li>
    <li>Suggesting endorsement, affiliation, or certification you do not have</li>
    <li>Modifying a mark — recolouring, distorting, adding to it — and continuing to present it as the brand's</li>
  </ul>


  <h2>For contributors</h2>

  <p>By submitting a logo you confirm:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>It came from an official source, which you have declared in the PR</li>
    <li>You are not aware of brand guidelines that forbid its redistribution</li>
    <li>You claim no ownership of the mark</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    If a brand kit explicitly forbids redistribution, <strong>do not submit the asset</strong>. Open
    an issue instead — the entity's metadata is still valuable, and the record can carry a
    <code>null</code> logo indefinitely.
  </p>

  <h2>For brand owners</h2>

  <p>
    If you own a mark in this dataset and want it changed or removed, open an issue titled
    <code>trademark: &lt;brand&gt;</code>. Requests are honoured — we will remove the asset without
    arguing the merits.
  </p>

  <p>Two things worth knowing before you ask:</p>

  <p>
    <strong>We would rather host your correct logo than have developers use a wrong one.</strong>
    Removal does not stop your mark appearing in Indian fintech products; it just means the version
    in circulation is a stale screenshot someone scraped. If your objection is to a specific outdated
    or distorted asset, sending us the current one solves the problem better than removal does.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Metadata is separate from artwork.</strong> We can drop the SVG and keep the factual
    record — name, category, IFSC prefix, website — which is public information. Tell us which you
    want.
  </p>

